finding. round_path chooses the next ordinal lane round filename, file_review writes only an accepted verdict as that round record when the round reader reads its lane path back as that lane's scope, and lane_commits resolves commits on a branch and requires the base to be an ancestor of the reviewed commit.\"","+detail = \"Round accepts only a full-lane review with no prior findings or a narrow review that names the prior findings file, and requires its test list. render_review strictly fills the shipped reviewer template with the work-item specification, lane range, test command, scratch location, optional review rubric and verdict destination; render_critique strictly fills the shipped critique template with the work-item specification and named rubric. Both refuse a missing specification, unreadable or empty named input, or unfilled template slot before a brief is written. review_refusal accepts only a verdict bound to the reviewed full commit with exactly one line whose keyword, in any case, is VERDICT, in exactly the canonical form `VERDICT: <APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED> findings=<digits>`, whose count matches its finding lines and whose changes request names a finding. round_path chooses the next ordinal lane round filename, file_review writes only an accepted verdict as that round record when the round reader reads its lane path back as that lane's scope and the record's directory is not the rollup generator's own, and lane_commits resolves commits on a branch and requires the base to be an ancestor of the reviewed commit.\""," rationale = \"An attended reviewer needs the same reviewed instructions and durable verdict carrier as an unattended review without inheriting its scheduler. Strict rendering and boundary validation prevent a reviewer from receiving incomplete instructions or an unrelated verdict from becoming review history.\""," test_refs = \"TC-333\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-852\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3389,"oldLines":9,"newStart":3389,"newLines":9,"lines":[" [test.TC-333]"," verifies = [\"SR-146\", \"SR-235\", \"LLR-313\", \"IF-288\", \"IF-289\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Run test_a_rendered_review_brief_carries_the_kit_clauses_and_the_lane_facts, test_a_narrow_round_names_the_findings_it_answers, test_a_narrow_round_without_findings_and_a_full_one_with_them_are_refused, test_a_named_input_that_is_not_there_refuses, test_an_unfilled_slot_refuses_and_no_brief_is_written, test_the_scope_critique_carries_ruling_twos_questions_and_its_rubric, test_a_filed_coordinator_review_appears_in_the_rollup, test_a_malformed_review_is_refused_and_nothing_is_filed, test_a_round_with_no_tests_refuses, test_an_empty_or_missing_named_input_refuses, test_the_critique_render_refuses_a_missing_spec, test_the_command_line_refuses_a_lane_the_git_reads_reject, test_a_review_render_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_brief, and test_filing_a_review_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_round_file. Render full and narrow review briefs and a scope critique over a temporary lane; refuse an empty test list, empty or missing named inputs, and a critique without a specification; on a real lane, drive detached, non-commit and non-ancestor command-line refusals, then successful review rendering and filing; file a well-formed review and malformed review cases, and attempt filing for a lane whose branch the round reader cannot read back as a review scope, before rendering the rollup.\"","+method = \"Run test_a_rendered_review_brief_carries_the_kit_clauses_and_the_lane_facts, test_a_narrow_round_names_the_findings_it_answers, test_a_narrow_round_without_findings_and_a_full_one_with_them_are_refused, test_a_named_input_that_is_not_there_refuses, test_an_unfilled_slot_refuses_and_no_brief_is_written, test_the_scope_critique_carries_ruling_twos_questions_and_its_rubric, test_a_filed_coordinator_review_appears_in_the_rollup, test_a_malformed_review_is_refused_and_nothing_is_filed, test_a_round_with_no_tests_refuses, test_an_empty_or_missing_named_input_refuses, test_the_critique_render_refuses_a_missing_spec, test_the_command_line_refuses_a_lane_the_git_reads_reject, test_a_review_render_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_brief, and test_filing_a_review_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_round_file. Render full and narrow review briefs and a scope critique over a temporary lane; refuse an empty test list, empty or missing named inputs, and a critique without a specification; on a real lane, drive detached, non-commit and non-ancestor command-line refusals, then successful review rendering and filing; file a well-formed review and malformed review cases, and attempt filing for a lane whose branch the round reader cannot read back as a review scope or whose branch names the rollup generator's own directory, before rendering the rollup.\""," tier = \"Smoke\"","-expected = \"A complete attended review or critique brief has no unfilled slot and carries the shipped review clauses, lane facts or scope rubric as applicable. An empty test list, invalid round shape, missing specification, unreadable or empty named input, unfilled template slot, malformed or unbound verdict, and a lane branch the round reader cannot read as a review scope are refused without a requested file or review record. A detached lane, non-commit revision or non-ancestor base returns exit 2 with no output file and a clean repository. A successful review returns exit 0 and writes only its brief with full resolved revisions and the reviewed tip; successful filing returns exit 0 and adds only the next review-round record. A valid filed review is rendered in the lane review history.\"","+expected = \"A complete attended review or critique brief has no unfilled slot and carries the shipped review clauses, lane facts or scope rubric as applicable. An empty test list, invalid round shape, missing specification, unreadable or empty named input, unfilled template slot, malformed or unbound verdict (without exactly one line whose keyword, compared case-insensitively, is VERDICT in the canonical form `VERDICT: <APPROVE|CHANGES-REQUESTED> findings=<digits>`), a lane branch the round reader cannot read as a review scope, and a lane whose scope is the rollup generator's own directory are refused without a requested file or review record. A detached lane, non-commit revision or non-ancestor base returns exit 2 with no output file and a clean repository. A successful review returns exit 0 and writes only its brief with full resolved revisions and the reviewed tip; successful filing returns exit 0 and adds only the next review-round record. A valid filed review is rendered in the lane review history.\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_rendered_review_brief_carries_the_kit_clauses_and_the_lane_facts; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_narrow_round_names_the_findings_it_answers; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_narrow_round_without_findings_and_a_full_one_with_them_are_refused; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_named_input_that_is_not_there_refuses; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_an_unfilled_slot_refuses_and_no_brief_is_written; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_the_scope_critique_carries_ruling_twos_questions_and_its_rubric; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_filed_coordinator_review_appears_in_the_rollup; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_malformed_review_is_refused_and_nothing_is_filed; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_a_round_with_no_tests_refuses; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_an_empty_or_missing_named_input_refuses; tests/test_review_brief.py::test_the_critique_render_refuses_a_missing_spec; tests/test_review_brief_git.py::test_the_command_line_refuses_a_lane_the_git_reads_reject; tests/test_review_brief_git.py::test_a_review_render_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_brief; tests/test_review_brief_git.py::test_filing_a_review_exits_zero_and_writes_only_the_round_file\""," statu